# What a remote build uploads from your working tree. CI checkouts carry none
# of this, so it only matters for a deploy run from your own machine; without
# it, node_modules and your local database ship to the builder.
#
# Patterns need the **/ prefix to reach into anu-tree-database/: a bare
# node_modules only matches the one at the root, and the app's own copy holds
# Windows binaries that would break the linux build.
.git
**/node_modules
**/.next
dist
.astro
.data
*.log
**/*.log
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.envrc
mise.local.toml
*.pem
**/*.pem
.claude

# the working copy of the database; the committed one at
# anu-tree-database/src/db/treedb.sqlite is the seed and must still ship
anu-tree-database/src/db/treedb copy.sqlite
